---
/**
 * 04 The Expanding Production Deck (Events): deployed in V1.3 from the V1.2
 * review checkpoint, in place of three sections (the Sui Summit session, the
 * production room and Sui Fest), and since V1.4 one full-width vertical
 * accordion at every width. Three chapters, PRODUCTION ROOM, EVENT FILM and
 * LIVE PRESENTATION (events.json `deck`; in that order since Full Site
 * Iteration V1.2, which leads with the strongest visual work, where the live
 * presentation had led), in one stack: every chapter's header always visible
 * and one chapter open at a time, the production room to begin with. The
 * order is the data's, so the numbers, the open chapter, the keyboard and focus
 * order, the scroll-assisted turns and the reading order all follow it. A
 * click or a tap on a header opens its chapter and closes the
 * other; each header is a button (Tab to it, Enter or Space opens it, the arrow
 * keys, Home and End move between them) with a strong focus ring, and the open
 * one, which cannot be closed into nothing, says so. Nothing advances by itself.
 * The open chapter's height eases open and the other's closes (a little over
 * half a second, no bounce), the chosen header never slipping under the site's
 * header; once they have, the opened chapter is brought into view if it is not.
 *
 * An open chapter is a substantial section: on wide screens its media and its
 * words side by side (the media 58% of the two columns, the words 42%), the
 * chapter about 70% of the screen's height unless its words need more, with
 * generous padding; on narrow ones the media above the words. The media: a
 * muted preview (an approved loop of 8 to 15 seconds; it plays only while it is
 * shown and well in view, never for reduced motion or a data-saving
 * preference, and has its own pause control), and, where the chapter has one,
 * the full film, which "Watch full video with sound" plays in place with its
 * sound and its controls (EvPlayer; one sound at a time, as everywhere on the
 * page). Since V1.5 the live presentation keeps only its preview. The words
 * (V1.5): the headline, the introduction, up to three things John did, the
 * outcome and the fine-print credit (with a second line naming the
 * participating teams where there are any). On wide screens they use the
 * column's full height: the headline near its top, the credit toward its
 * bottom, the space between the groups growing with the room the chapter has
 * (within bounds, so nothing drifts apart), the media centered beside them.
 * Collapsed headers carry only their number, title and a chevron.
 *
 * The production room (V1.4, events.json `setupFinal`) opens on Final (since
 * Creator Marketing V1.2, Part One; it opened on Setup before): the finished
 * explainer's muted preview, which plays by itself while the chapter is open
 * and in view, with its pause control. A segmented control just above the
 * stage (V1.5: two equal options, SETUP and FINAL, the selected one filled in
 * the accent) switches the same stage to Setup, the behind-the-scenes
 * photograph, and back, through a crossfade; the reader makes the switch, the
 * stage keeps its size, and the two are never side by side. The reader's last
 * choice holds for the rest of the visit: closing the chapter and opening it
 * again does not bring Final back over a chosen Setup. Watch full video with
 * sound shows only under Final; under Setup its line stays empty, so nothing
 * below moves.
 *
 * Reduced motion: a chapter changes through a short fade, with no height in
 * motion and no scroll pinning, and Setup and Final change at once. Without
 * JavaScript all three chapters are open, each film with its native controls,
 * and the production room shows its film, then its photograph; a chapter with
 * no film (V1.6: the live presentation and the event film) shows its preview
 * still, on its poster.
 *
 * V1.6. The words keep V1.5's generous spacing but now run in a natural
 * top-to-bottom rhythm from the same top line as the media: nothing is
 * stretched to the media's height or centered against it, and the band between
 * a chapter's header and its content is about a fifth smaller than the space
 * the centering left above the live presentation's headline. The headers keep
 * their stable labels (01 PRODUCTION ROOM and so on); the long headline stays
 * in the words. Since the Creator Marketing V1.0 brief (Part I), the live
 * presentation's and the event film's video sits in the vertical center of the
 * open card, with balanced room above and below; the words still start at the
 * top, and the production room keeps its Setup and Final on the top line.
 *
 * The media carry the hero's production vocabulary, quieter: restrained corner
 * marks just outside the active frame and a small timecode at its top right
 * that reads the clip's own playback (it shows once the clip has played and
 * follows it, paused or running; there is none over the setup photograph).
 * They belong to the frame that is shown, so a closed chapter has none. The
 * live presentation's preview is the hero's own presentation edit, in its own
 * wide frame, and the event film's is the hero's Sui Fest edit; only the
 * production room has a film with sound, under Final.
 *
 * Scroll-assisted (wide screens with motion allowed, tall enough to hold a
 * chapter): the deck pins just below the site's header and the reader's own
 * scrolling moves it on. The production room is open as the deck arrives
 * (V1.2); further scrolling opens the event film, then the live presentation, each after
 * a clear viewing interval (about six tenths of a screen of scrolling), and
 * scrolling back up reverses the sequence. A chapter that does not fit the room
 * left on screen first moves up with the scroll until its foot is in view, then
 * holds; the header after it shows below it where there is room, and otherwise
 * waits below the edge, so the open chapter's own header stays clear of the
 * site's header (only a chapter taller than the room passes it on the way to its
 * foot). After the live presentation's interval the deck lets go and the page
 * carries on into the conclusion. Nothing snaps, nothing
 * waits for a video to end, and nothing takes the reader's input: a click, a
 * tap or the keyboard opens any chapter at once (while the deck is pinned, the
 * page's position moves with it, unseen, so scrolling carries on from that
 * chapter). Reduced motion, narrow screens and short ones keep the manual
 * accordion above.
 */
import events from '@data/events.json';
import { getAsset } from '@lib/assets';
import { clockLabel } from '@lib/ev-copy';
import Icon from '@components/Icon.astro';
import EvPlayer from './EvPlayer.astro';
import EvSlot from './EvSlot.astro';

const { deck, setupFinal, hero } = events;
const pad = (n: number) => String(n).padStart(2, '0');
const chapters = deck.chapters.map((ch, i) => {
  const full = ch.full ? getAsset(ch.full) : null;
  return { ...ch, num: pad(i + 1), length: full?.duration ? clockLabel(full.duration) : '', sf: ch.key === setupFinal.chapter ? setupFinal : null };
});
// The fine print keeps its names whole (V1.5): in every credit the name after "by"
// stays with it (V1.6, now that a later credit can carry one too); every short
// credit after the first stays on one line (a span that never wraps, so not even at
// a hyphen); each separator stays with the words before it; each team in a list of
// participants stays whole.
const NBSP = '\u00a0';
const whole = (part: string) => part.replace(/ by ([^,]+)$/, (_, name: string) => ` by${NBSP}${name.replaceAll(' ', NBSP)}`);
const credit = (t: string) => t.split(' · ').map((part, i) => ({ text: whole(part), keep: i > 0 && part.length <= 34 }));
const teams = (t: string) => t.split(', ').map((item) => item.split(' and ').map((name) => name.replaceAll(' ', NBSP)).join(' and ')).join(', ');
// The media column: about 58% of the content on wide screens, the whole width on narrow ones.
const sizes = '(min-width: 90rem) 760px, (min-width: 64rem) 56vw, 100vw';
---

<section class="evd" id="ev-deck" data-surface="dark" aria-labelledby="ev-deck-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="ev-deck-title" class="sr-only">{chapters.map((c) => c.label).join(', ')}</h2>
    {/* The runway (V1.6): with the scroll-assisted deck it is as tall as the deck and
        its scrolling, and the deck pins inside it; otherwise it is just the deck. */}
    <div class="evd__runway" data-deck-runway>
      <div class="evd__deck" data-ev-deck>
        <div class="evd__row">
          {
            chapters.map((ch, i) => (
              <article class:list={['evd__ch', i === 0 && 'is-open']} data-deck-ch={ch.key}>
                <h3 class="evd__h">
                  <button type="button" class="evd__rail" id={`ev-deck-rail-${ch.key}`} aria-expanded={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls={`ev-deck-${ch.key}`} data-deck-rail>
                    <span class="evd__num">{ch.num}</span>{' '}
                    <span class="evd__label">{ch.label}</span>
                    <span class="evd__chev" aria-hidden="true" />
                  </button>
                </h3>
                <div class="evd__body" id={`ev-deck-${ch.key}`} role="region" aria-labelledby={`ev-deck-rail-${ch.key}`}>
                  <div class="evd__clip">
                    <div class="evd__content">
                      <div class:list={['evd__media', !ch.sf && 'evd__media--centered']}>
                        {ch.sf ? (
                          <div class="evd__sf" data-sf>
                            <div class="evd__sf-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label={ch.sf.label} data-sf-tabs>
                              <button type="button" role="tab" class="evd__sf-tab" id="ev-sf-tab-setup" aria-controls="ev-sf-setup" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-sf-tab="setup">
                                {ch.sf.tabs.setup}
                              </button>
                              <button type="button" role="tab" class="evd__sf-tab" id="ev-sf-tab-final" aria-controls="ev-sf-final" aria-selected="true" data-sf-tab="final">
                                {ch.sf.tabs.final}
                              </button>
                            </div>
                            {/* The stage: Setup and Final share it, and its frame marks and
                                timecode belong to whichever is shown. */}
                            <div class="evd__frame evd__frame--sf" data-deck-frame>
                              <div class="evd__sf-panel" id="ev-sf-setup" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="ev-sf-tab-setup" data-sf-panel="setup" data-loop-off>
                                <EvSlot id={ch.sf.photo} aspect="16:9" sizes={sizes} class="evd__photo" />
                              </div>
                              <div class="evd__sf-panel is-shown" id="ev-sf-final" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="ev-sf-tab-final" data-sf-panel="final">
                                <div class="evd__preview" data-deck-preview>
                                  <EvSlot id={ch.preview} aspect="16:9" fit={ch.previewFit === 'contain' ? 'contain' : 'cover'} class="evd__loop" />
                                </div>
                                {ch.full && (
                                  <div class="evd__full" data-deck-full>
                                    <EvPlayer id={ch.full} label={ch.fullLabel} aspect="16:9" domId={`ev-deck-player-${ch.key}`} class="evd__player" />
                                  </div>
                                )}
                              </div>
                              <span class="evd__mark evd__mark--tl" aria-hidden="true" />
                              <span class="evd__mark evd__mark--tr" aria-hidden="true" />
                              <span class="evd__mark evd__mark--bl" aria-hidden="true" />
                              <span class="evd__mark evd__mark--br" aria-hidden="true" />
                              <span class="evd__tc" aria-hidden="true" data-deck-tc>
                                <span class="evd__tc-key">{hero.monitor.timecode}</span>
                                <span data-deck-tc-value>00:00:00:00</span>
                              </span>
                            </div>
                          </div>
                        ) : (
                          <div class:list={['evd__frame', ch.full && 'evd__frame--full']} data-deck-frame>
                            <div class="evd__preview" data-deck-preview>
                              {/* `native`: the preview in its own frame (the live presentation's
                                  wide recording, as the hero shows it); otherwise 16:9. */}
                              <EvSlot id={ch.preview} aspect={ch.previewFit === 'native' ? undefined : '16:9'} fit={ch.previewFit === 'contain' ? 'contain' : 'cover'} class="evd__loop" />
                            </div>
                            {ch.full && (
                              <div class="evd__full" data-deck-full>
                                <EvPlayer id={ch.full} label={ch.fullLabel} aspect="16:9" domId={`ev-deck-player-${ch.key}`} class="evd__player" />
                              </div>
                            )}
                            <span class="evd__mark evd__mark--tl" aria-hidden="true" />
                            <span class="evd__mark evd__mark--tr" aria-hidden="true" />
                            <span class="evd__mark evd__mark--bl" aria-hidden="true" />
                            <span class="evd__mark evd__mark--br" aria-hidden="true" />
                            <span class="evd__tc" aria-hidden="true" data-deck-tc>
                              <span class="evd__tc-key">{hero.monitor.timecode}</span>
                              <span data-deck-tc-value>00:00:00:00</span>
                            </span>
                          </div>
                        )}
                        {/* Only where the chapter has a film (V1.6: the production room
                            alone); there it belongs to FINAL, out of sight under SETUP. */}
                        {ch.full && (
                          <button type="button" class="evd__watch" data-deck-watch>
                            <span class="evd__watch-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                              <Icon name="play" size={12} />
                            </span>
                            <span>{deck.watch}</span>
                            {ch.length && <span class="evd__len">{ch.length}</span>}
                          </button>
                        )}
                      </div>
                      {/* The words, with a spacer between each group (empty, decorative):
                          see "the words" below. */}
                      <div class="evd__text">
                        <h4 class="display evd__title">{ch.headline}</h4>
                        <span class="evd__gap evd__gap--lead" aria-hidden="true" />
                        <p class="evd__context">{ch.context}</p>
                        <span class="evd__gap" aria-hidden="true" />
                        <ul class="evd__points">
                          {ch.points.map((p) => (
                            <li>{p}</li>
                          ))}
                        </ul>
                        <span class="evd__gap" aria-hidden="true" />
                        {ch.outcomeLabel ? (
                          <div class="evd__callout">
                            <p class="evd__callout-label"><span class="evd__callout-icon"><Icon name="flag" size={14} /></span><span>{ch.outcomeLabel.split(' ').map((w, i) => (<>{i > 0 && ' '}<span class="evd__keep-word">{w}</span></>))}</span></p>
                            <p class="evd__outcome">{ch.outcome.split('**').map((part, i) => (i % 2 === 1 ? <strong>{part}</strong> : part))}</p>
                          </div>
                        ) : (
                          <p class="evd__outcome">{ch.outcome}</p>
                        )}
                        <span class="evd__gap" aria-hidden="true" />
                        <div class="evd__credits">
                          <p class="evd__credit">
                            {credit(ch.credit).map((part, i) => (
                              <>
                                {i > 0 && `${NBSP}· `}
                                {part.keep ? <span class="evd__keep">{part.text}</span> : part.text}
                              </>
                            ))}
                          </p>
                          {ch.participants && <p class="evd__credit evd__credit--with">{teams(ch.participants)}</p>}
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import { mountLoops, mountPlayers, players, timecode } from '@lib/ev-media';

  const reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
  const pauseAll = (scope: ParentNode) => {
    for (const v of Array.from(scope.querySelectorAll('video'))) if (!v.paused) v.pause();
  };

  // ---- the frame's timecode (V1.6) -------------------------------------------------------
  // It reads the clip that is shown in the frame: its own playback, frame by frame
  // while it runs and held where it stops. It shows once that clip has played; over
  // the setup photograph, or a clip that has not started, there is none.
  const mountTimecode = (frame: HTMLElement) => {
    const out = frame.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-deck-tc-value]');
    const videos = Array.from(frame.querySelectorAll('video'));
    if (!out || !videos.length) return;
    const shown = (v: HTMLVideoElement) => !v.closest('[data-sf-panel]:not(.is-shown), [data-deck-preview][hidden], .evd__full:not(.is-shown)');
    let raf = 0;
    let last = '';
    const render = () => {
      raf = 0;
      const v = videos.find(shown) ?? null;
      const running = Boolean(v && (!v.paused || v.currentTime > 0));
      frame.classList.toggle('is-running', running);
      if (v) {
        const t = timecode(v.currentTime);
        if (t !== last) {
          out.textContent = t;
          last = t;
        }
        if (!v.paused && !v.ended) raf = requestAnimationFrame(render);
      }
    };
    const kick = () => {
      if (!raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(render);
    };
    for (const v of videos) for (const type of ['play', 'playing', 'pause', 'seeked', 'timeupdate', 'loadeddata', 'ended']) v.addEventListener(type, kick);
    frame.addEventListener('ev:frame-sync', kick);
    kick();
  };

  for (const deck of Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ev-deck]'))) {
    mountPlayers(deck);
    mountLoops(deck);
    const frames = Array.from(deck.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-deck-frame]'));
    frames.forEach(mountTimecode);
    const chapters = Array.from(deck.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-deck-ch]'));
    const rails = chapters.map((ch) => ch.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-deck-rail]') as HTMLButtonElement);
    const section = deck.closest<HTMLElement>('.evd');
    const runway = deck.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-deck-runway]');

    // One chapter open at a time, and always one: the open chapter's header cannot
    // close it into nothing, and says so (aria-disabled). A chapter that closes
    // pauses whatever plays in it (a film keeps its place for the reader's return).
    let current = 0;
    const open = (index: number) => {
      current = index;
      chapters.forEach((ch, k) => {
        const on = k === index;
        ch.classList.toggle('is-open', on);
        rails[k].setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(on));
        if (on) rails[k].setAttribute('aria-disabled', 'true');
        else rails[k].removeAttribute('aria-disabled');
        if (!on) pauseAll(ch);
      });
    };
    open(Math.max(0, chapters.findIndex((ch) => ch.classList.contains('is-open'))));

    // ---- the manual accordion (reduced motion, narrow or short screens) -----------------
    // While the heights change, the header the reader chose moves up as the chapter
    // above it closes, but never under the site's header: if it would, the page
    // follows it. Once the heights have settled, the opened chapter is brought into
    // view if it is not: the least scrolling that shows all of it, or, if it is
    // taller than the screen, its header just below the site's header.
    const floor = () => parseFloat(getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).scrollPaddingTop) || 88;
    const reveal = (ch: HTMLElement) => {
      const top = floor();
      const r = ch.getBoundingClientRect();
      const bottom = window.innerHeight - 16;
      let dy = 0;
      if (r.top < top) dy = r.top - top;
      else if (r.bottom > bottom) dy = r.height <= bottom - top ? r.bottom - bottom : r.top - top;
      if (Math.abs(dy) >= 1) window.scrollBy({ top: dy, behavior: reduce.matches ? 'instant' : 'smooth' });
    };
    const settle = (ch: HTMLElement, rail: HTMLElement) => {
      const t0 = performance.now();
      const span = reduce.matches ? 0 : 600;
      const step = (now: number) => {
        const dy = rail.getBoundingClientRect().top - floor();
        if (dy < -1) window.scrollBy({ top: dy, behavior: 'instant' });
        if (now - t0 < span) requestAnimationFrame(step);
        else reveal(ch);
      };
      requestAnimationFrame(step);
    };

    // ---- the scroll-assisted deck (V1.6) --------------------------------------------------
    // On wide screens with motion allowed (and room for a chapter), the deck pins just
    // below the site's header, inside a runway as long as its scrolling. Measured in
    // pixels of scrolling since the runway's top reached the pin line (u), each
    // chapter has its turn: first any reveal (a chapter taller than the room on screen
    // moves up with the scroll until its foot is in view), then its viewing interval,
    // when nothing moves; at the end of a turn the next chapter opens. The browser's
    // own sticky positioning does the moving: for the open chapter the deck starts its
    // turn at the pin line (a lead above it in the runway equal to where its turn
    // starts) and sticks once its foot is in view (a pin line raised by what does not
    // fit). The reader's scrolling is never taken over or snapped: going back up runs
    // the same turns in reverse, and once the last interval has passed the deck lets go.
    type Plan = { pin: number; over: number[]; starts: number[]; end: number };
    let plan: Plan | null = null;
    let pinned = false;
    let derived = -1;
    let raf = 0;
    let flip = 0;
    const MIN_H = 640;
    const rem = () => parseFloat(getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).fontSize) || 16;
    const canPin = () => Boolean(section && runway) && !reduce.matches && deck.clientWidth >= 56 * rem() && window.innerHeight >= MIN_H;
    const measure = (): Plan => {
      const row = deck.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.evd__row');
      const gap = row ? parseFloat(getComputedStyle(row).rowGap) || 0 : 0;
      // Every header (with its chapter's border) and the gaps between them, plus the
      // one open chapter's content: the deck's height with each chapter open.
      const head = chapters.map((ch) => (ch.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.evd__h')?.offsetHeight ?? 0) + (ch.offsetHeight - ch.clientHeight));
      const heads = head.reduce((sum, h) => sum + h, 0) + gap * (chapters.length - 1);
      const tall = chapters.map((ch) => heads + (ch.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.evd__content')?.offsetHeight ?? 0));
      const top = floor() + 16;
      const room = window.innerHeight - top - 24;
      // On a tall screen the deck sits in the middle of the room it has, by its tallest
      // chapter, so it never moves as the chapters change.
      const pin = Math.round(top + Math.max(0, (room - Math.max(...tall)) / 2));
      // What is in view while chapter k holds: all of it down to its foot, and the
      // header after it (the way on) while the chapter's own header can stay clear of
      // the site's header; on a shorter screen the header after it waits below the
      // edge instead. Only what does not fit scrolls into view before the chapter
      // holds (a chapter taller than the room passes its own header under the site's
      // header on the way to its foot, as any long section does), so a header never
      // goes under the site's header to show headers further down.
      const after = (k: number) => head.slice(k + 2).reduce((sum, h) => sum + h + gap, 0);
      const above = (k: number) => head.slice(0, k).reduce((sum, h) => sum + h + gap, 0);
      const next = (k: number) => (k < chapters.length - 1 ? head[k + 1] + gap : 0);
      const over = tall.map((h, k) => {
        const withNext = Math.max(0, Math.round(h - after(k) - room));
        if (pin - withNext + above(k) >= floor()) return withNext;
        return Math.max(0, Math.round(h - after(k) - next(k) - room));
      });
      const hold = Math.round(Math.min(640, Math.max(360, window.innerHeight * 0.6)));
      const starts = [0];
      over.forEach((o, k) => starts.push(starts[k] + o + hold));
      const end = starts[chapters.length];
      // Long enough that the deck lets go exactly at the end of the last interval.
      const last = chapters.length - 1;
      if (runway) runway.style.height = `${end + tall[last] - over[last]}px`;
      return { pin, over, starts, end };
    };
    const progress = () => (plan && runway ? plan.pin - runway.getBoundingClientRect().top : 0);
    const turn = (u: number) => {
      let k = 0;
      while (plan && k < chapters.length - 1 && u >= plan.starts[k + 1]) k += 1;
      return k;
    };
    // Where the deck rides for chapter k's turn.
    const place = (k: number) => {
      if (!plan) return;
      deck.style.setProperty('--deck-lead', `${plan.starts[k]}px`);
      deck.style.setProperty('--pin-top', `${plan.pin - plan.over[k]}px`);
    };
    // A change of chapter while pinned moves the deck to its new place; it eases there
    // (over the same half second as the heights) rather than jumping.
    const move = (change: () => void) => {
      // Where the reader sees it now (with any easing still under way), then its new
      // place without any offset; the difference is eased away.
      const before = deck.getBoundingClientRect().top;
      window.clearTimeout(flip);
      deck.classList.remove('is-shifting');
      deck.style.removeProperty('--deck-y');
      change();
      const dy = before - deck.getBoundingClientRect().top;
      if (Math.abs(dy) < 1) return;
      deck.style.setProperty('--deck-y', `${Math.round(dy)}px`);
      void deck.offsetHeight;
      deck.classList.add('is-shifting');
      deck.style.setProperty('--deck-y', '0px');
      flip = window.setTimeout(() => {
        deck.classList.remove('is-shifting');
        deck.style.removeProperty('--deck-y');
      }, 620);
    };
    const update = () => {
      raf = 0;
      if (!pinned || !plan) return;
      const k = turn(progress());
      if (k === derived) return;
      const first = derived < 0;
      derived = k;
      if (first) {
        if (current !== k) open(k);
        place(k);
      } else {
        move(() => {
          if (current !== k) open(k);
          place(k);
        });
      }
    };
    const queue = () => {
      if (pinned && !raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(update);
    };
    const setMode = () => {
      const want = canPin();
      if (want !== pinned) {
        pinned = want;
        section?.classList.toggle('is-pinned', want);
        derived = -1;
        if (!want) {
          plan = null;
          if (runway) runway.style.height = '';
          for (const v of ['--deck-y', '--deck-lead', '--pin-top']) deck.style.removeProperty(v);
          return;
        }
      }
      if (!pinned) return;
      plan = measure();
      if (derived >= 0) place(derived);
      queue();
    };
    setMode();
    window.addEventListener('scroll', queue, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('resize', setMode, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('pageshow', setMode);
    reduce.addEventListener?.('change', setMode);
    document.fonts?.ready.then(setMode).catch(() => {});

    rails.forEach((rail, i) => {
      rail.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (chapters[i].classList.contains('is-open')) return;
        if (pinned && plan) {
          // Pinned: the chapter opens at once, and the page's position moves to the
          // start of its turn (unseen: the deck stays where the reader is looking), so
          // the reader's scrolling carries on from it. Before or after the pinned
          // stretch it simply opens.
          const u = progress();
          const ready = plan;
          move(() => {
            open(i);
            if (u >= 0 && u <= ready.end) {
              derived = i;
              place(i);
              window.scrollTo({ top: window.scrollY + (ready.starts[i] + 1 - u), behavior: 'instant' });
            }
          });
          return;
        }
        open(i);
        settle(chapters[i], rail);
      });
      rail.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
        const n = rails.length;
        const to = ({ ArrowDown: i + 1, ArrowRight: i + 1, ArrowUp: i - 1, ArrowLeft: i - 1, Home: 0, End: n - 1 } as Record<string, number>)[event.key];
        if (to === undefined) return;
        event.preventDefault();
        rails[(to + n) % n].focus();
      });
    });

    // The production room's Setup and Final: a segmented control over one stage.
    // The reader switches; the panel that leaves stays beneath until the one that
    // arrives has faded in over it. Leaving Final pauses what plays there, and its
    // preview loop waits (data-loop-off) until Final shows again. Watch full video
    // with sound belongs to Final: under Setup it steps out of sight (is-away),
    // its line kept, so nothing below moves.
    for (const sf of Array.from(deck.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-sf]'))) {
      const list = sf.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sf-tabs]');
      const tabs = Array.from(sf.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-sf-tab]'));
      const panels = Array.from(sf.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-sf-panel]'));
      const frame = sf.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-deck-frame]');
      const watch = sf.closest('[data-deck-ch]')?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-deck-watch]');
      if (!list || !tabs.length) continue;
      const select = (key: string, focus = false) => {
        for (const t of tabs) {
          const on = t.dataset.sfTab === key;
          t.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(on));
          t.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1;
          if (on && focus) t.focus();
        }
        for (const p of panels) {
          const on = p.dataset.sfPanel === key;
          p.classList.toggle('is-shown', on);
          p.toggleAttribute('data-loop-off', !on);
          if (!on) pauseAll(p);
          for (const loop of Array.from(p.querySelectorAll('[data-ev-loop]'))) loop.dispatchEvent(new Event('ev:loop-sync'));
        }
        watch?.classList.toggle('is-away', key !== 'final');
        sf.dataset.view = key;
        frame?.dispatchEvent(new Event('ev:frame-sync'));
      };
      tabs.forEach((t, i) => {
        t.addEventListener('click', () => select(t.dataset.sfTab as string));
        t.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
          const k = event.key;
          if (k !== 'ArrowRight' && k !== 'ArrowLeft' && k !== 'Home' && k !== 'End') return;
          event.preventDefault();
          const j = k === 'Home' ? 0 : k === 'End' ? tabs.length - 1 : (i + (k === 'ArrowRight' ? 1 : -1) + tabs.length) % tabs.length;
          select(tabs[j].dataset.sfTab as string, true);
        });
      });
      // Final first (V1.2); afterwards the reader's last choice stands for the visit.
      select('final');
    }

    // Watch full video with sound: the preview steps aside and the full film plays
    // in its place, with sound and its controls (the reader's press allows the
    // sound). Only the production room has one, under Final.
    for (const ch of chapters) {
      const watch = ch.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-deck-watch]');
      const preview = ch.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-deck-preview]');
      const full = ch.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-deck-full]');
      watch?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        preview?.querySelector('video')?.pause();
        if (preview) preview.hidden = true;
        full?.classList.add('is-shown');
        watch.hidden = true;
        ch.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-deck-frame]')?.dispatchEvent(new Event('ev:frame-sync'));
        const root = full?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-evp]');
        if (!root) return;
        players.get(root.id)?.begin();
        root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-evp-play]')?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
      });
    }
  }
</script>

<style>
  .evd {
    --deck-ease: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
    --deck-pad: clamp(1.5rem, 3.2cqi, 2.75rem);
    --head-h: 4.25rem;
    padding-block: var(--section-y);
    /* The deck places the chosen header itself while heights change. */
    overflow-anchor: none;
  }

  .evd__deck {
    container: deck / inline-size;
  }

  /* ---- the scroll-assisted deck (V1.6) ------------------------------------------------
     The runway holds the deck and, when it pins, the length of its scrolling (set by
     the script); its own formatting context keeps the deck's lead inside it. The
     deck sticks at its pin line for the open chapter's turn (both set by the script)
     and eases to a new place when the chapter changes. */
  .evd__runway {
    display: flow-root;
  }

  .evd.is-pinned .evd__deck {
    position: sticky;
    top: var(--pin-top, 6.5rem);
    margin-top: var(--deck-lead, 0px);
    transform: translate3d(0, var(--deck-y, 0px), 0);
  }

  .evd.is-pinned .evd__deck.is-shifting {
    transition: transform 0.55s var(--deck-ease);
  }

  /* One stack, at every width. */
  .evd__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  /* ---- a chapter: its header, then its body ------------------------------------------- */
  .evd__ch {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    transition: border-color var(--dur) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .evd__ch.is-open {
    border-color: var(--line-strong);
  }

  .evd__h {
    display: flex;
    margin: 0;
    font: inherit;
  }

  /* The header: compact, the whole of it the button; its number, its title and a
     chevron that turns as the chapter opens. */
  .evd__rail {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 3.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    color: var(--heading);
    font: 700 var(--text-xs) / 1.3 var(--font-sans);
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-align: left;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .evd__ch:not(.is-open) .evd__rail:hover {
    background: var(--bg-sunk);
  }

  .evd__ch.is-open .evd__rail {
    cursor: default;
  }

  .evd__rail:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--focus);
    outline-offset: -5px;
    border-radius: calc(var(--radius-lg) - 2px);
  }

  .evd__num {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .evd__chev {
    width: 0.6rem;
    height: 0.6rem;
    margin-left: auto;
    border-right: 1.5px solid var(--ink-3);
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--ink-3);
    transform: translateY(-2px) rotate(45deg);
    transition:
      transform var(--dur) var(--ease-out),
      border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .evd__ch:not(.is-open) .evd__rail:hover .evd__chev {
    border-color: var(--accent-ink);
  }

  .evd__ch.is-open .evd__chev {
    transform: translateY(2px) rotate(225deg);
  }

  :global(html:not(.js)) .evd__chev {
    display: none;
  }

  .evd__clip {
    min-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* A little room above the media (V1.6), so the frame's top marks show. */
  .evd__content {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.15rem 1.35rem;
  }

  /* ---- the media: the preview, or the full film in its place -------------------------- */
  .evd__media {
    container: media / inline-size;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    align-content: start;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .evd__media :global(.ev-slot),
  .evd__media :global(.evp__frame) {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  /* ---- the frame: the active media and its production marks (V1.6) --------------------
     The hero's vocabulary, quieter: four corner marks just outside the frame
     (smaller and fainter than the hero's) and, at its top right, a small timecode
     reading the clip that is shown. Only with JavaScript, and only on the frame of
     the open chapter (a closed one is not drawn at all); the player's own corner
     marks give way to these inside the deck. No label, tally, scan lines or
     controls are added. */
  .evd__frame {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .evd__mark,
  .evd__tc {
    display: none;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__mark {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 2;
    display: block;
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-color: rgba(237, 240, 239, 0.2);
    border-style: solid;
    border-width: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__mark--tl {
    left: -0.5rem;
    top: -0.5rem;
    border-left-width: 1px;
    border-top-width: 1px;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__mark--tr {
    right: -0.5rem;
    top: -0.5rem;
    border-right-width: 1px;
    border-top-width: 1px;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__mark--bl {
    left: -0.5rem;
    bottom: -0.5rem;
    border-left-width: 1px;
    border-bottom-width: 1px;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__mark--br {
    right: -0.5rem;
    bottom: -0.5rem;
    border-right-width: 1px;
    border-bottom-width: 1px;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__frame :global(.evp__crop) {
    display: none;
  }

  /* The timecode: the hero's reading (TC and the clip's own time), a size smaller
     and quieter, on a faint shade so it holds over any picture. It shows once the
     clip has played (is-running) and fades with it. */
  :global(html.js) .evd__tc {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.55rem;
    right: 0.55rem;
    z-index: 3;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5em;
    padding: 0.3em 0.55em;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: rgba(13, 15, 16, 0.55);
    color: #b9c0c1;
    font: 600 0.625rem / 1.2 var(--font-sans);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    white-space: nowrap;
    pointer-events: none;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
  }

  .evd__tc-key {
    color: #8a949c;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__frame.is-running .evd__tc {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* The smallest frames: the timecode steps aside (the marks stay). */
  @container media (max-width: 18rem) {
    :global(html.js) .evd__tc {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  .evd__watch {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-self: start;
    white-space: nowrap;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem 0.6rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--heading);
    font: 600 var(--text-sm) / 1 var(--font-sans);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
      border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .evd__watch:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--bg-sunk);
  }

  .evd__watch:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--focus);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .evd__watch-icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.5rem;
    height: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--c-ink);
  }

  .evd__len {
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  /* The smallest phones: the label a touch smaller and the film's length left to
     the player, so the button stays on one line within its column. */
  @container deck (max-width: 21rem) {
    .evd__watch {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
    }

    .evd__len {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /* With JavaScript the full film waits behind its preview until it is asked for;
     without it, where a chapter has a film, there is no preview, only the film with
     its native controls, and where it has none (V1.6: the live presentation and the
     event film) the preview stands still on its poster frame. */
  :global(html.js) .evd__full:not(.is-shown) {
    display: none;
  }

  :global(html:not(.js)) .evd__frame--sf .evd__preview,
  :global(html:not(.js)) .evd__frame--full .evd__preview,
  :global(html:not(.js)) .evd__watch {
    display: none;
  }

  /* In the production room, Watch belongs to Final: under Setup it is out of
     sight and out of reach (visibility), its line kept so nothing below moves, and
     it fades back with Final. */
  :global(html.js) .evd__watch.is-away {
    visibility: hidden;
    opacity: 0;
    transition:
      opacity 0.2s ease,
      visibility 0s linear 0.2s;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__sf ~ .evd__watch:not(.is-away) {
    transition:
      opacity 0.35s ease,
      visibility 0s linear 0s,
      background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
      border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  /* ---- the production room's Setup and Final (V1.4; the control since V1.5) ----------- */
  .evd__sf {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /* Without JavaScript: the film, then the photograph (V1.2), and no control. */
  :global(html:not(.js)) .evd__frame--sf {
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  :global(html:not(.js)) .evd__sf-panel[data-sf-panel='final'] {
    order: -1;
  }

  :global(html:not(.js)) .evd__sf-tabs {
    display: none;
  }

  /* A clear segmented control, just above the stage at every width: two equal
     options in one track, the selected one filled in the accent (dark type on it,
     5.3:1), the other quiet until it is hovered. The whole control is a
     comfortable target for a finger (2.75rem tall). */
  .evd__sf-tabs {
    justify-self: start;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 3px;
    width: min(100%, 16rem);
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    padding: 3px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(237, 240, 239, 0.26);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--bg-sunk);
  }

  .evd__sf-tab {
    min-height: 2.25rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 1rem;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font: 700 0.75rem / 1 var(--font-sans);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      background-color 0.2s var(--ease-out),
      color 0.2s var(--ease-out);
  }

  .evd__sf-tab:hover {
    color: var(--heading);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--heading) 9%, transparent);
  }

  .evd__sf-tab[aria-selected='true'] {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--c-ink);
    cursor: default;
  }

  .evd__sf-tab:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--heading);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* With JavaScript the two share one stage (one grid cell, as tall as the taller,
     so nothing moves when they change): the panel arriving fades in over the one
     leaving, which stays beneath it until it is covered. */
  :global(html.js) .evd__sf-panel {
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
    min-width: 0;
    opacity: 0;
    visibility: hidden;
    transition:
      opacity 0s linear 0.35s,
      visibility 0s linear 0.35s;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__sf-panel.is-shown {
    z-index: 1;
    opacity: 1;
    visibility: visible;
    transition:
      opacity 0.35s ease,
      visibility 0s linear 0s;
  }

  /* ---- the words (V1.5; V1.6 a natural rhythm) -------------------------------------------
     Five groups, each with room around it: the headline, the introduction, the
     things John did, the outcome, and the fine-print credit. The gaps are spacers
     of their own, a fixed size each (V1.6: the generous spacing V1.5 gave them,
     but never stretched to fill the media's height, and nothing centers the words
     against it): the words simply run from the top. */
  .evd__text {
    --gap-lead: 0.9rem;
    --gap: 1.35rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .evd__gap {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    height: var(--gap);
  }

  .evd__gap--lead {
    height: var(--gap-lead);
  }

  .evd__title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    color: var(--heading);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .evd__context {
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .evd__points {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .evd__points li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.9rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .evd__points li::before {
    content: '';
    width: 0.38rem;
    height: 0.38rem;
    margin-top: 0.55em;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .evd__outcome {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 0.85rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--heading);
  }

  /* V1.3: a labeled outcome (Commercial Follow-Through). V1.5: a proof card, a thin teal outline with a
     restrained radius and a faint teal-tinted fill, the label and its flag in one row above the copy. The
     credit stays below, outside the card. */
  .evd__callout {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: clamp(1rem, 0.85rem + 0.5vw, 1.35rem) clamp(1.05rem, 0.9rem + 0.6vw, 1.5rem);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, transparent);
    border-radius: 0.625rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, transparent);
  }

  /* V1.6: the card's copy carries two approved bold phrases, a step heavier
     than its already semibold text. */
  .evd__callout .evd__outcome strong {
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .evd__callout .evd__outcome {
    padding-left: 0;
    border-left: 0;
  }

  .evd__callout-label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .evd__callout-icon {
    display: inline-grid;
    flex: none;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.875rem;
    height: 1.875rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 60%, transparent);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, transparent);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* A hyphenated word in the label never breaks at its hyphen. */
  .evd__keep-word {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .evd__callout-icon :global(svg) {
    display: block;
  }

  /* The fine print: the credit line, and the participating teams on a line of
     their own where a chapter has them. */
  .evd__credits {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }

  .evd__credit {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .evd__keep {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .evd__credit--with {
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* ---- with JavaScript: one chapter open at a time -------------------------------------- */
  /* The open chapter's height eases open and the closing one's eases shut (a
     restrained curve, no bounce); its content fades in a moment behind. */
  :global(html.js) .evd__body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 0fr;
    visibility: hidden;
    transition:
      grid-template-rows 0.55s var(--deck-ease),
      visibility 0s linear 0.55s;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__ch.is-open .evd__body {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
    visibility: visible;
    transition:
      grid-template-rows 0.55s var(--deck-ease),
      visibility 0s linear 0s;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__content {
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  :global(html.js) .evd__ch.is-open .evd__content {
    opacity: 1;
    transition: opacity 0.35s ease 0.12s;
  }

  /* ---- wide (the deck 56rem or more): a substantial section ---------------------------- */
  @container deck (min-width: 56rem) {
    .evd__rail {
      min-height: var(--head-h);
      gap: 1rem;
      padding: 1.1rem var(--deck-pad);
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
    }

    /* The media 58% of the two columns, the words 42%, both from one top line (V1.6:
       the chapter is as tall as its content, with no minimum and no centering), a
       measured band below the header (about a fifth less than the space V1.5's
       centering left above the live presentation's headline). */
    .evd__content {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 58fr) minmax(0, 42fr);
